<title>RUSSIA: Russia 357-day T-bill yields 34.44 percent.</title>
<headline>Russia 357-day T-bill yields 34.44 percent.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The annualised average yield on an issue of 357-day GKO discount Treasury bills was 34.44 percent at an auction on Wednesday, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>The 23002 issue, which matures on February 18, 1998, the closest maturity date for the new issue, closed at 75.55 percent to yield 34.34 percent on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Dealers had forecast the yield would be in a 33.01-36.00 percent range.</p>
<p>Full details of the auction follow:</p>
<p>    Series number		   23003</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denominations		   1.00 million</p>
<p>    Bids (nominal)		 11.97 trln</p>
<p>    Sold (nominal)		  5.75 trln</p>
<p>    Proceeds			  4.30 trln</p>
<p>    Average price		   74.80 pct</p>
<p>    Lowest accepted price	 74.51 pct</p>
<p>    Average yield		   34.44 pct</p>
<p>    Highest accepted yield	34.98 pct</p>
<p>    Tenor			     357 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   March 4, 1998</p>
<p>On March 12 the Finance Ministry will also auction four trillion roubles in 168-day T-bills (series 22071), repay about 375.58 billion roubles in interest on an OFZ government bond (series 24007) and repay 6.92 trillion roubles in maturing 133-day T-bills (series 22056).</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
